ArchangelOS-authored parts of this repository (build system, GUI installer,
category launcher, welcome window, SDDM/lockscreen theme, branding and
configuration) are MIT-licensed. Everything ArchangelOS bundles into the
generated ISO images remains under its own upstream license; this NOTICE
credits those projects. Inclusion here is attribution, not a claim of
ownership or endorsement by the upstreams.

================================================================================
Base system & tooling
================================================================================
- Arch Linux and pacman — https://archlinux.org
  Package sets are pulled from the official core/extra/multilib repositories.
- archiso (ISO build framework) — https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/archiso
- Linux kernel — https://kernel.org (GPL-2.0)

================================================================================
Additional package repositories
================================================================================
- BlackArch Linux — https://blackarch.org
  The Fallen (RedTeam) edition enables the [blackarch] repository and installs
  BlackArch tool groups. BlackArch is bootstrapped via strap.sh and mirrored
  from the public BlackArch mirror network, including:
    ftp.halifax.rwth-aachen.de, mirrors.ocf.berkeley.edu, mirror.yandex.ru,
    mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn, mirror.team-cymru.com, www.blackarch.org
  All BlackArch tools retain their individual upstream licenses.
- Chaotic-AUR — https://aur.chaotic.cx
  Prebuilt AUR binaries used to install applications that are not in the
  official repositories. Served from cdn-mirror.chaotic.cx and
  builds.garudalinux.org.
- Arch User Repository (AUR) — https://aur.archlinux.org
  Some applications are built at image-build time via an AUR helper.

================================================================================
Desktop shell & environment
================================================================================
- ArcShell (Quickshell-based Hyprland desktop shell) — sud0-L
  https://github.com/sud0-L/arcshell
  Cloned and installed at build time; provides the shell/launcher experience
  layered under ArchangelOS.
- Hyprland (Wayland compositor) — https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland
- Quickshell — https://github.com/quickshell-mirror/quickshell
- SDDM (display manager) — https://github.com/sddm/sddm
- Qylock (Quickshell lockscreen) — Darkkal44
  https://github.com/Darkkal44/qylock
  The ArchangelOS lockscreen reuses the SDDM theme under Qylock's shim.
- Rio terminal — https://github.com/raphamorim/rio

