================================================================================
Security tooling (Fallen / RedTeam edition)
================================================================================
The RedOps toolset is installed from a mix of the official repositories,
BlackArch, the AUR/Chaotic-AUR, language ecosystems (PyPI, Go, npm, crates.io)
and upstream Git repositories. Each tool is the property of its respective
authors and is distributed under its own license. Notable frameworks cloned
directly from source include (non-exhaustive):
  Sliver (BishopFox), Havoc (HavocFramework), Mythic (its-a-feature),
  Empire/Starkiller (BC-SECURITY), PoshC2 (nettitude), Merlin (Ne0nd0g),
  SILENTTRINITY (byt3bl33d3r), MITRE Caldera (mitre), Atomic Red Team
  (redcanaryco), NimPlant (chvancooten), Villain (t3l3machus),
  HexStrike AI (0x4m4), PentestGPT (GreyDGL), the ProjectDiscovery suite,
  PEASS-ng (carlospolop), PayloadsAllTheThings (swisskyrepo) and
  SecLists (danielmiessler).

These tools are provided for authorized security testing, research and
education only. Users are responsible for complying with all applicable laws
and for having explicit authorization before testing any system.

================================================================================
Applications
================================================================================
The Home, Gaming and Fallen editions bundle a large set of desktop and CLI
applications from the Arch repositories, AUR/Chaotic-AUR and upstream sources
(browsers, office suites, creative tools, media apps, developer tools, game
launchers, and more). Each application is distributed under its own license
by its respective authors.

